 # relux-mcp
 
-Curator MCP declaration packages (`agent-mcp.json`) for Relux agent environments. Packages live under `packages/<name>/`.
+Private MCP declaration packages, version **1.0.0**, for Curator's
+agent-environments protocol. No tags are created by this delivery; the
+orchestrator cuts reviewed release tags.
+
+| Package | Transport | Declaration |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| figma | HTTP | https://mcp.figma.com/mcp |
+| safari | stdio | safaridriver-mcp --mcp |
+
+Source: agents-infra commit
+`459742ea67e3c6b84169520b92d74fe7f73e3002`,
+`.configs/codex-mcp-servers.toml`. There is no shared LLDB definition at
+that pin: upstream dropped lldb-mcp, so this repository has **no LLDB package**.
+
+## Machine policy and credentials
+
+Source URL: `git@github.com:relux-works/relux-mcp.git`, addressed at
+`packages/figma` and `packages/safari`. The canonical network source
+identity is `github.com/relux-works/relux-mcp`; operators must permit this
+identity in the machine MCP package allowlist (segment-aware source matching).
+The allowlist authorizes package sources, not executable names. Network
+acquisition policy must also permit that repository. No machine policy or home
+files are changed here.
+
+Both declarations carry `env_names: []`: the pinned source declares no bearer
+token. Authentication is handled by the client's remote MCP authentication
+flow. If an integration later needs a bearer token, declare only its environment
+variable name through `env_names` and supply the value from the operator's
+environment; never put values in arguments, URLs, headers, or package files.
+That change requires revising the release gate and validating client support.
+
+## Safari wrapper and PATH
+
+`bin/safaridriver-mcp` is a POSIX sh wrapper that forwards every argument with
+`exec` to Safari Technology Preview's safaridriver. Requires macOS, Safari
+Technology Preview 247+, Web Developer features and remote automation/external
+agents enabled. A missing or non-executable driver produces a diagnostic and
+exit 127.
+
+The deployment owner must expose this wrapper through a command in the
+machine-current profile's skill command set: its machine forwarding shim in
+the manager's user-bin directory must resolve `safaridriver-mcp`, and that
+directory must be on PATH. MCP declarations do not install commands themselves.
+Shipping this wrapper is not an installation of that shim. Revision 1 inherits
+machine-current shims even for launches of another profile; profile-local
+`path_prepend` is reserved and is not used here. For checkout-only validation,
+an operator can put this repository's `bin` directory on PATH.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run `scripts/validate.sh` (Python 3 required), then
+`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v`.
+The gate checks exactly the two pinned release declarations, strict JSON keys,
+identity/version, bare command, and exact credential-free URL/arguments.
+It is intentionally a release inventory gate, not a general protocol parser
+or arbitrary-secret detector. Tests drive the shell entry point and narrow
+three guard classes to measure test sensitivity. The producer evidence includes
+an independent Curator `internal/contextpkg.ParseMCP` oracle (the declaration
+parser; `internal/mcp` checks already-configured servers).
